meta {
  name: 14 Stream Live Logs
  type: http
  seq: 14
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/logs/applications?level=info
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  level: info
  ~device_id: {{demoDeviceId}}
  ~application_id: 1
  ~kind: device
}

headers {
  Accept: text/event-stream
}

docs {
  `GET /logs/stream` — live SSE firehose of device and application logs.
  Bruno renders the events as they arrive; **leave this running in its own
  tab** for the rest of the demo.
  
  - `level` is a *minimum severity* filter (`trace|debug|info|warn|error|fatal`).
    Mid-demo trick: change it to `error`, re-send, and the noise disappears.
  - Enable `device_id` / `kind` to narrow to one device or to
    `device` vs `application` logs only.
  
  Each event is JSON tagged with its kind, e.g.
  `{"kind":"device","id":"…","time":"…","device_id":1,"level":"info","message":"…","source":"…"}`.
}
